       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Single dose:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** Four doses of 1600 mg is 6400 mg/day. The maximum for inpatient use is 3200 mg/day, and the OTC limit is 1200 mg/day. At 6400 mg/day, the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1600 mg/day)\n- 600 mg PO four times daily (2400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want, and add any note you'd like on the order, such as \"take with food.\" I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll flag it with a note, but I'd advise against it."
