       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily (6400 mg/day) is double the maximum daily dose. I don't know of any indication that supports it, and it would put the patient at serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. Confirming doesn't change that risk.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily (2400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily (1600 mg/day)\n\nIf you need more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than these give, I'd suggest talking with pharmacy about adding a second agent, such as scheduled acetaminophen, instead of raising the ibuprofen dose.\n\nIf you think the dose is justified, you can place the order yourself directly in the order-entry system, where pharmacy verification can review it."
